# 1. PROJECT VISION

Develop a digital platform named:

**MUMBAI CIVIC DATA INTELLIGENCE PORTAL**

Subtitle: BMC Data Management, Smart Locality Analytics & Business Connect.

The main purpose is to transform scattered or differently formatted municipal information into a structured, searchable, reliable and analysable information system.

The project should also use organised locality information to help residents discover local businesses and help participating retailers improve their digital visibility.

The platform must have three major components:

### MODULE 1 — BMC DATA INTELLIGENCE

- Collect publicly available BMC information.
- Extract data from PDF, Excel and CSV files.
- Clean and standardise inconsistent information.
- Categorise data by ward and department.
- Store structured information in a central database.
- Show source documents and original records.
- Compare ward-level statistics.
- Generate meaningful data insights.
- Provide downloadable datasets and reports.

### MODULE 2 — POWER BI & ADVANCED ANALYTICS

- Build professional interactive Power BI reports.
- Connect Power BI with the cleaned and structured dataset.
- Use Power Query for transformations.
- Use DAX for calculated measures.
- Develop ward-wise analytics and detailed comparisons.
- Create interactive reports using slicers, bookmarks, drill-through and report tooltips.
- Display Power BI reports within the website where supported.
- Provide standalone `.pbix` files for offline demonstration.
- Generate data-quality and business-impact reports.

### MODULE 3 — LOCAL BUSINESS CONNECT

- Allow local retailers to register.
- Allow consumers to discover nearby businesses.
- Provide searchable business categories.
- Display business information and products or services.
- Allow consumers to send enquiries.
- Measure business visibility and engagement.
- Provide business-owner analytics.
- Calculate estimated business benefits using actual retailer-provided information.

The three components must work together through common locality, ward and business-category information where appropriate.

IMPORTANT:

This is an academic prototype, not an official BMC application. Do not falsely claim BMC affiliation, endorsement or direct live integration.

Display: "Academic Community Engagement Project | Independent Prototype".

